    "question": "Locate current complete defaultWide8 costs after accepted CPP657 and unchanged cached source through TED698, before selecting a materially different redesign from CWO697 overlap trial.",
    "sourceFinding": "Horizontal geometry is prepared once; source rows are converted once per cache ID, with no redundant full-row copy. Narrow ordinary versus mixed writers have different row addressing: mixed rows are padded for aligned Vector512 views; ordinary odd-width rows are not. Do not unify their indexing blindly or add generic pixel abstractions.",
    "scope": "Existing513x259to128x64byte completeResize, exact managed/rational/frozen frames and original native max1/RMSE.25. Native retains graph/scratch as labeled. Reuse harness, fixture and actualpackageWindowsDLL; no source/build/test/qualification/timing repeat. One2second CPU0operation/CPU1sampler capture, instrumentedelapseddiscarded; locations/skid notphasecosts.",
    "prior": "CGA654 precedes accepted pixel preparation; CWO697 has no useful complete lead and exact restoration. No overlap-loop variant or failed microoptimization replay.",
    "next": "Map current hot regions, distinguish preparation/conversion/filtering/certification/repair and select a substantial coherent hypothesis only if supported. Stop passing paths; no blanket release refresh or global text block.",
    "finding": {
      "locations": {
        "total": 1773,
        "cachedDriver": 906,
        "horizontalTapGroupIG64": 735,
        "widePublication": 434,
        "premultiplyDecode": 207,
        "originalRepair": 126,
        "kernel": 14
      },
      "meaning": "Exclusive sampled locations and skid, not phase times, stall proof or projected savings. Geometry/session preparation is not established as a material CPU opportunity. Instrumented elapsed discarded."
    },
    "nextHypothesis": {
      "removedWork": "For contiguous private clamped horizontal windows, replace two checked variable decoded-pixel indexes per tap with checked bounded spans before the tap traversal. Keep independent ordered accumulators; no overlap-load sharing.",
      "endState": "One source window per output with identical ordered Multiply/Add, original weights/normalizers/offsets for repair, and the existing irregular/clamped/unequal-padding fallback. No new heap, owner, cache, session or public API.",
      "eligibilityProofRequired": "Private offsets are Clamp(first+t). Equal counts with endpoint difference n-1 establish a contiguous window; unequal padded counts retain original path. Slice/loop bounds must remain safe on odd, clamped, single, full-capacity and arbitrary nonfixture dimensions.",
      "risks": "JIT may keep range checks, added eligibility branches/spans may offset savings, or code growth may regress companions. Verify actual generated code rather than infer from source. Keep portable fallback and exact floating operation order.",
      "workloads": "Existing complete Wide8 first; independent confirmation only for useful completed-stage evidence, then all seven affected byte/word support32/64/128/256 companions. Exact frozen/rational/native gates, ownership/admission and bounded cancellation; no new image/settings grid.",
      "decisionRule": "No automatic merge or numerical-policy change. Focused normal/scalar checks, complete short and independent confirmation if justified; broad W/L/live/affectedISA/SAMEpackage once at accepted coherent milestone. Do not repeat adverse measurements for favorable results.",
      "relationToPrior": "CPP657 removes repeated channel interpretation; CWO697 shares overlapping loads without a useful lead. This design instead bounds the contiguous range before indexing; it is not a replay of either implementation."
    }
  },
